  "summary": "The distinctive Spanish satirical drawing style known as 'tonchi', characterized by loose, expressive line work and humorous social commentary.",
  "description": "This style appears relaxed yet purposeful, with fluid lines and simplified forms that capture Spanish social types and political figures with affectionate satire. It developed through Spain's satirical press tradition, particularly in publications like 'La Codorniz' and 'Hermanos de la Fragua', and represents a uniquely Spanish approach to caricature that blends observation with local humor.",
